I have to say I am really delighted by Hearse. On my first encounter
with it, I was attacked by a warhorse on entering lvl 4 or 5. I threw
it the lichen I'd been carrying, and then noticed there was a ghost in
the room with me. Once the warhorse had killed it, I noticed that
there was another ghost, which the horse also killed for me. Two
graves in the room, each killed by a warhorse, pretty cool, given how
little trouble it had caused me. In the next room I found the previous
owner of the warhorse, killed by a black unicorn, which was no concern
of mine, since my char was chaotic. This lead to my best ever
character, which died on the bottom level of the mines, attacking a
cockatrice while polymorphed to a centaur (the killing kick did us
both in, and my lizard was no use since I wasn't hissed at). I was
impressed as heck that I should be the fourth player to walk through
the bones level...
In my current game, the first level of the mines (dlvl 3) was a bones
file, this time containing two graves (killed by a gnome lord while
helpless and some other rather sad death while helpless), one of which
contained Magicbane, some +2 gloves and a cursed dilithium crystal,
which I converted to 4 points of protection. This character is looking
really good at the moment, although I used up all my personal (Real
Life) luck when I weilded Magicbane without testing it -- it was
uncursed, as were the gloves, although I had enough sense to test
those before putting them on.
Bones files, particularly those at shallow depths, seem rather a good
leg up. Do people, other than Marvin, ascend very often without any
help from bones files?

